  "Number": 41,
  "Question": "The sum of all the roots of \\(4x^3-8x^2-63x-9=0\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(8\\)",
    "B": "\\(2\\)",
    "C": "\\(-8\\)",
    "D": "\\(-2\\)",
    "E": "\\(0\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The sum of the roots can be found without solving the cubic. Let its roots, counted with multiplicity, be \\(\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma\\). Then\n\\[\n4x^3-8x^2-63x-9\n=4(x-\\alpha)(x-\\beta)(x-\\gamma).\n\\]\nTo obtain an \\(x^2\\) term from the product, we choose the constant from exactly one factor and \\(x\\) from the other two. Therefore its coefficient is\n\\[\n-4\\alpha-4\\beta-4\\gamma\n=-4(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma).\n\\]\nComparing this with the given coefficient \\(-8\\),\n\\[\n\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma=\\frac{-8}{-4}=2.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{2}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
